  "body": "Found by mkinney's QA runs (p02, p03, p04, p05, p08) and reproduced on a minimal part by a separate verification run on 2026-11-18, CamCraft main `83867fd7` (= v0.24.0 code). Minimal repro projects and posted programs are kept on mkinney's machines and can be attached.\n\nWhat happens (Tormach 770MX + microARC 4, the documented per-operation `tilt` route of the microARC tester kit, #785): `tilt {a_deg: 180}` is refused (\"Tool axis A must be in -90..90 ... for the face opposite the top, use Tool axis A 0 and Tool axis B 180\"). Written as A0/B180, the op posts `G0 A180` correctly, but its XY is turned 90 degrees: a slot programmed from (10,0) to (30,0) posts as\n```\nG0 A180\nG1 X0 Y-10 Z24.5 F300\nG1 X0 Y-30 Z24.5 F400\n```\ni.e. along Y at the bar's end face (X0), not along X at X10-30. The same slot at A90 and A-90 posts X10 -> X30 correctly. No reading of B180 as an A-only index maps local X to machine Y.\n\nWhy P1: wrong posted G-code for a 4th-axis index that passes verify and posts.\n\nDone means: on an A-only machine, a 180-degree index posts the same local XY as the untilted op (pinned by a test with A0/A90/A-90/A180 slots), and the refusal text names the A-only way to reach A180.\n",
